@host = https://localhost:7001

### Get all products (page 1, default page size)
GET {{host}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

### Get product by id
GET {{host}}/api/products/1
Accept: application/json

### Get all brands
GET {{host}}/api/products/brands
Accept: application/json

### Get all types
GET {{host}}/api/products/types
Accept: application/json

### Filter by brand
GET {{host}}/api/products?brandId=2
Accept: application/json

### Filter by type
GET {{host}}/api/products?typeId=1
Accept: application/json

### Filter by brand AND type together
GET {{host}}/api/products?brandId=2&typeId=1
Accept: application/json

### Search by name
GET {{host}}/api/products?search=jacket
Accept: application/json

### Sort by price descending
GET {{host}}/api/products?sort=priceDesc

### Sort by price ascending
GET {{host}}/api/products?sort=priceAsc

### Pagination - page 2, 4 products per page
GET {{host}}/api/products?pageIndex=2&pageSize=4

### Combine everything - search + sort + paging
GET {{host}}/api/products?search=shirt&sort=priceAsc&pageIndex=1&pageSize=5

### --- Basket endpoints (need Redis running - see README) ---

### Get basket (nothing saved yet -> returns an empty basket, not an error)
GET {{host}}/api/baskets?id=test-basket-1

### Create or update a basket
POST {{host}}/api/baskets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "test-basket-1",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Classic White T-Shirt",
      "pictureUrl": "images/products/ClassicWhiteTShirt.jpeg",
      "price": 120,
      "quantity": 2
    }
  ]
}

### Get the basket again - should now return the items we just saved
GET {{host}}/api/baskets?id=test-basket-1

### Delete the basket
DELETE {{host}}/api/baskets/test-basket-1
